<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>HTTP Methods and Status Codes</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: #f4f7fb;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 20px;
        }
        h1 {
            text-align: center;
            color: #2c3e50;
        }
        h2 {
            color: #34495e;
            margin-top: 25px;
        }
        .section {
            background: #ffffff;
            padding: 15px;
            margin: 15px 0;
            border-left: 6px solid #27ae60;
            box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
        }
        ul {
            margin-top: 10px;
        }
        table {
            width: 100%;
            border-collapse: collapse;
            margin-top: 20px;
            background: #ffffff;
        }
        th, td {
            border: 1px solid #ccc;
            padding: 10px;
            text-align: left;
        }
        th {
            background-color: #27ae60;
            color: white;
        }
        code {
            background: #eee;
            padding: 8px;
            display: block;
            margin-top: 8px;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>HTTP Methods and Status Codes</h1>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>What is an HTTP Method?</h2>
        <p>An HTTP Method tells the server what action the client wants to perform.</p>
        <code>GET /users HTTP/1.1</code>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>Common HTTP Methods</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><b>GET</b> – Retrieve data from server.</li>
            <li><b>POST</b> – Create new resource.</li>
            <li><b>PUT</b> – Update entire resource.</li>
            <li><b>PATCH</b> – Update partial resource.</li>
            <li><b>DELETE</b> – Remove resource.</li>
            <li><b>HEAD</b> – Returns headers only.</li>
            <li><b>OPTIONS</b> – Shows allowed methods.</li>
            <li><b>CONNECT</b> – Establish tunnel.</li>
            <li><b>TRACE</b> – Debug request.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>HTTP Methods Summary</h2>
        <table>
            <tr>
                <th>Method</th>
                <th>Purpose</th>
                <th>Changes Data?</th>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>GET</td>
                <td>Retrieve data</td>
                <td>No</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>POST</td>
                <td>Create data</td>
                <td>Yes</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>PUT</td>
                <td>Update full resource</td>
                <td>Yes</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>PATCH</td>
                <td>Update partial resource</td>
                <td>Yes</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>DELETE</td>
                <td>Remove data</td>
                <td>Yes</td>
            </tr>
        </table>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>HTTP Status Codes</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><b>1xx</b> – Informational (100 Continue)</li>
            <li><b>2xx</b> – Success (200 OK, 201 Created)</li>
            <li><b>3xx</b> – Redirection (301 Moved Permanently)</li>
            <li><b>4xx</b> – Client Errors (400 Bad Request, 404 Not Found)</li>
            <li><b>5xx</b> – Server Errors (500 Internal Server Error)</li>
        </ul>

        <code>
HTTP/1.1 200 OK<br>
Content-Type: application/json
        </code>
    </div>

</body>
</html>
